From: HP-UX 11.23 ia64 port notes
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] diagnostic: let libbacktrace find the executable via GCC_BT_EXE

DIAGNOSTIC / NOT A FIX. libbacktrace cannot locate the running executable on
HP-UX, so an ICE backtrace is empty. Reading the path from GCC_BT_EXE makes
backtraces work while debugging the port. Not needed by a shipping compiler.
--- a/gcc/diagnostic.c
+++ b/gcc/diagnostic.c
@@ -530,7 +530,14 @@
       {
 	struct backtrace_state *state = NULL;
 	if (diag_kind == DK_ICE)
-	  state = backtrace_create_state (NULL, 0, bt_err_callback, NULL);
+	  {
+	    /* DIAGNOSTIC HACK (not for shipping): passing NULL makes libbacktrace locate the
+	       executable itself, which fails on HP-UX 11.23 - there is no /proc/self/exe, so every
+	       ICE prints "libbacktrace could not find executable to open" and no frames.  Allow the
+	       path to be supplied out-of-band so we can get a symbolised backtrace on this host.  */
+	    const char *btexe = getenv ("GCC_BT_EXE");
+	    state = backtrace_create_state (btexe, 0, bt_err_callback, NULL);
+	  }
 	int count = 0;
 	if (state != NULL)
 	  backtrace_full (state, 2, bt_callback, bt_err_callback,
